From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:17:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 141/145] fix(witness): move the worktree reap off pre_start
 into mol-witness-patrol (gcp-d9uj)

The reaper was the witness pre_start, which gascity SIGKILLs at
[session] setup_timeout, so it held itself to 8s. Under load that was one
bead read and nothing else (ferth 10-06: 1 of 35 examined; winnow 10-07:
bead_query_timed_out), so real removal armed for winnow could not make
progress. A patrol step has no start deadline, so the budget becomes a
policy choice instead of a survival constraint.

reap-merged-worktrees now runs the script itself. It resolves it from the
formula's own source path (gc formula list --json) with GC_PACK_DIR as the
fallback only (gcp-amo), the same way audit-polecat-homes does, so the old
"a formula step cannot name a pack asset" claim is removed. agent.toml
drops the pre_start: exactly one reaper runs per cycle.

Two per-rig vars, set in [rigs.formula_vars]: worktree_reap_mode (default
dry-run; only the exact word "remove" passes --no-dry-run, anything empty,
unknown or unrendered is dry-run) and worktree_reap_budget (default 120,
capped at 540 to stay inside a shell tool's 10-minute cap). An unresolvable
script or missing rig is a loud FINDING and a non-zero fence status, never a
silent exit 0.

Tests: new test_witness_reap_wiring.sh (12 cases; resolution order, loud
failure, mode and budget parsing, and end-to-end runs of the real script over
12 closed-bead worktrees in dry-run and armed). test_agent_pre_start_budget,
test_gastown_pack_assets and test_polecat_worktree_reap are retargeted from
the pre_start to the patrol wiring. Untested in situ: var rendering on a
root-only poured wisp; the fence falls back to dry-run/120 and prints an
INFO line when a placeholder arrives unrendered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
